<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>This 13-day Silk Road group tour is our most popular itinerary, taking you through three of China's most legendary provinces. From the vibrant Sunday Market in Kashgar to the rainbow mountains of Zhangye and the mirror-like Chaka Salt Lake, every day brings a new wonder. Travel with a small group (max 16), stay in comfortable 4-star hotels, and enjoy the expertise of our English-speaking guides.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Explore Kashgar's legendary Sunday Market</li><li>Drive the Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</li>
      <li>Visit the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li><li>Camel ride at Singing Sand Dunes</li>
      <li>Walk the Jiayuguan Fortress</li><li>Rainbow Mountains at Zhangye Danxia</li>
      <li>Photograph Chaka Salt Lake at sunset</li><li>Tibetan culture experience in Xining</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Kashgar</h4><p>Arrive at Kashgar Airport. Your guide will meet you and transfer to your hotel. Free time to explore the Old City and enjoy local Uyghur cuisine.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Market & Old City</h4><p>Experience the legendary Kashgar Sunday Market — a centuries-old trading hub. Visit the Id Kah Mosque, the largest in China, and wander through the maze-like alleys of the Old City. Afternoon visit to Abakh Khoja Tomb.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Karakoram Highway to Taxkorgan</h4><p>Drive along the stunning Karakoram Highway. Visit Karakul Lake at 3,600m, with panoramic views of Muztagh Ata (7,546m). Arrive in Taxkorgan, China's westernmost town.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Taxkorgan 3★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Taxkorgan — Stone Fort → Return to Kashgar</h4><p>Visit the ancient Stone Fort and the grasslands. Return to Kashgar via the Karakoram Highway, stopping at scenic viewpoints.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Kashgar 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar ✈ Urumqi</h4><p>Morning flight to Urumqi. Visit the Xinjiang Regional Museum to see the famous Tarim mummies. Afternoon at Hongshan Park for panoramic city views.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Urumqi → Turpan</h4><p>Drive to Turpan (3 hours), the second-lowest depression on Earth. Visit the ancient Jiaohe Ruins and the ingenious Karez underground irrigation system.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan → Dunhuang (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning visit to the Flaming Mountains and Grape Valley. Afternoon high-speed train to Dunhuang (approx. 4 hours).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>Full UNESCO day. Morning at the Mogao Caves (8 caves included). Afternoon camel ride and sand surfing at the Singing Sand Dunes. Optional sunset at Crescent Moon Spring.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang → Jiayuguan</h4><p>Drive to Jiayuguan (5 hours) through the Gobi Desert. Visit the Jiayuguan Fortress, the western end of the Great Wall of China.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Jiayuguan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan → Zhangye</h4><p>Morning visit to the Overhanging Great Wall. Drive to Zhangye (2.5 hours). Late afternoon at Zhangye Danxia — the famous rainbow-colored rock formations, best photographed at sunset.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Zhangye 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangye → Xining (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning at the Giant Buddha Temple. High-speed train to Xining (approx. 3 hours). Visit Dongguan Mosque and stroll through the Muslim quarter.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Xining — Chaka Salt Lake</h4><p>Drive to Chaka Salt Lake (4 hours), the "Mirror of the Sky." Walk on the salt flats and capture stunning reflection photos. Visit Kumbum Monastery on the return journey.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Xining 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Xining</h4><p>Free time until your airport transfer. Your Silk Road adventure concludes. 再见!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>12 nights 4-star hotel accommodation (twin-share)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>English-speaking guide throughout</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All domestic flights & high-speed trains</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Private air-conditioned vehicle & driver</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Meals as indicated (B=Breakfast, L=Lunch, D=Dinner)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All entrance fees & listed activities</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Airport transfers on arrival & departure</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Travel insurance (China domestic)</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>What's Excluded</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>International flights to/from China</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Chinese visa fees</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Personal expenses & tips</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Single room supplement ($480)</p></div>
    </div>

